Patch 6503: the DualSense (PS5 controller, also the Edge) over USB or Bluetooth, from the v0.15 port. Windows has no
XInput driver for it, so with INPUT_MODE=controller the game fell back to the keyboard. A reader thread opens it as a
raw HID device (vendor 054C, product 0CE6 / 0DF2; Bluetooth is switched to the full report by reading feature report
0x05) and keeps the newest input report; port 0 uses it when XInput has no controller there, turned into an
XINPUT_STATE so the PAD_BTN_* rebinds apply (Cross = A, Circle = B, Square = X, Triangle = Y, Create = BACK,
Options = START). Also while port 0's empty-slot recheck is pending. PAD_NO_DUALSENSE=1 turns it off. Links setupapi
and hid (system DLLs). No rumble or lightbar.

Tested (US disc): see the J-Stars STATUS entry for the feature build with this patch.

